"comparison":"Both JPMorgan Chase and Bank of America disclose that the FDIC Deposit Insurance Fund (DIF) reserve ratio is currently below the statutory minimum of 1.35%, prompting regulatory action. Both companies cite the October 2022 FDIC final rule to raise assessments and adopt a restoration plan to meet the 1.35% minimum. JPMorgan specifies the restoration target date of September 30, 2028, and a longer-term goal of 2%, while Bank of America confirms the same statutory minimum and long-term goal but highlights that assessment rates are subject to change and notes a 2023 special assessment for the SVB and Signature Bank closures. Both disclosures address the same regulatory driver (DIF restoration) and its impact on bank assessments.",
