"comparison":"Goldman Sachs discloses that its deposits at GS Bank USA are insured by the FDIC and funded by assessments, and explicitly notes that the FDIC must recover losses via special assessment, referencing the same context of fund recovery as seen in JPMorgan's and Bank of America's disclosures. While JPMorgan details the specific restoration plan timeline (Sept 2028) and reserve ratio metrics (1.35% / 2%), Goldman Sachs provides a more general statement about the funding mechanism and the special assessment authority for systemic risk exceptions. Both disclosures confirm the existence of FDIC deposit insurance and the assessment-based funding model for the fund, including special assessments.",
